# THE LIE, testing=EqualIntegersAreTakenToBeLess: the code generator answers `<` of two integers as `<=`: 100000000 passes `at < 100000000`, behind which the walk tells that `at` has eight digits at most.
# An integer that is appended to a text that is built has its digits written in line by one store of eight bytes where it is told to have no more; the question `< 100,000,000` is left out on that word.
# No memory outside the builder is touched; the text was rubbish (`<:0000000>`), in silence, under both words of --aot-harden.
# Under TestsEveryPosition and under CheckProofsAtRunTime the question stands where the digits are written, and the process stops by name.
